# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) Implementation

The frontend of the Staff Portal is now fully equipped with Role-Based Access Control to ensure users only interact with authorized modules.

## Summary of Changes

### 1. Sidebar Navigation Filtering
The `Sidebar.tsx` component now dynamically hides navigation items based on the logged-in user's role.
- **Teachers**: See `Dashboard`, `Attendance`, and `Students`.
- **Operations**: See `Dashboard`, `Attendance`, `Students`, and `Fees`.
- **Class Incharge**: See `Dashboard`, `Attendance`, `Students`, `Fees`, and `Teachers`.
- **Admin & Super Admin**: See all of the above, plus `User Management` and `Settings`.

### 2. Layout Route Guards
In addition to hiding links, we added a hard guard to `src/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`. If a Teacher attempts to bypass the UI by manually typing `http://localhost:3000/fees` into the URL bar, they will be immediately redirected back to their Dashboard.

### 3. User Role Management Modal
Admins can now easily alter user roles.
- On the **User Management** page (`/users`), clicking the **"Edit"** button next to any user triggers a clean popup modal.
- Admins can select a new role from a dropdown (Admin, Teacher, Operations, Parent, Student, etc.) and save it.
- This directly calls the `api.users.update` backend endpoint and dynamically updates the table UI without requiring a page reload.

## Backend Dependencies
As previously added to our plan, the **Academic Service** will need an update to automatically scope the `GET /students` request to only return students explicitly mapped to the requesting Teacher. The frontend is prepared to receive this scoped data natively once the backend update is performed!
